--TEST--
a reference to an instance method through its class name, from a frame with no `$this`, is refused where it becomes a callable, and allowed where it is a link's target, which calls nothing — `rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`, `rule:routing/link-target-and-params-are-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A callable made from `Ledger::total` would have to keep the object the
// method runs on, and there is none here. `nvs_ir::lower::expr` reads the
// frame's `$this` for that object, so the refusal below is what stands between
// that read and a panic.
class Ledger {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/total", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function total(): string {
        return "2";
    }
}

// Legal: a link reads the route of the method and calls nothing.
echo Core\Router::url(Ledger::total), "\n";
callable $total = Ledger::total;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0778]: `Ledger::total` is not `static`, so a reference to it needs an object
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
